# Milestone: M3
# Covers: stopif(cond) body — terminates body no later than its end when
#         condition becomes true; Event-based and variable-change variants.
# defer-to: M5 (requires stopif keyword, reactive runtime, Event type, every keyword)
#
# Reason:
#   'stopif' is a reactive construct requiring the full reactive runtime (watcher
#   active polling, condition re-evaluation) — scheduled for M5.  The fixture
#   also uses the Event type with emission lifetime (~1s), 'every|(1s)' reactive
#   loop (M5), and ',' separator for concurrent observation (M5 chk driver).
#
# Original urbiscript (activate at M5+ with reactive runtime and Event type):
# # stopif(false) { echo("foo"); sleep(1s); echo("bar") }; echo("baz");
# # [00000001] *** foo
# # [00000002] *** bar
# # [00000003] *** baz
# # ... (see legacy/repos/aldebaran-urbi/tests/2.x/stopif.chk)
